---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const image = [
  'curl "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/barcodes/render"',
  '-H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"',
  '-H "Content-Type: application/json"',
  '--data \'{"value":"3017620422003","symbology":"ean13","format":"svg"}\'',
  '--output barcode.svg',
].join(" \\\n  ");
const labels = JSON.stringify({paper:"a4",items:[{value:"3017620422003",symbology:"ean13",title:"Sample product",detail:"SKU-001",copies:2}]},null,2);
const csv = JSON.stringify({csv_text:"barcode,sku\n3017620422003,ITEM-001\n"},null,2);
---
<DocsLayout title="Barcode Generation, PDF Labels & CSV Enrichment API | BarcodeNest" description="Generate barcode SVG and PNG images, render printable PDF labels and enrich barcode CSV files. API examples, account-wide monthly quotas and usage headers." heading="Generate images, print labels and enrich product files." intro="Use your API key or the signed-in website tools with separate account-wide allowances for each service." current="tools">
  <section><h2>Generate a barcode image</h2><p>Send <code>POST /v1/barcodes/render</code> with <code>value</code>, <code>symbology</code> and <code>format</code>. Symbology can be <code>ean13</code>, <code>upca</code>, <code>code128</code> or <code>qr</code>. Format can be <code>svg</code> or <code>png</code>. The response is the image itself.</p><CodeBlock label="Generate and save an SVG" language="bash" code={image} /><p>EAN-13 requires 13 digits and UPC-A requires 12 digits, including the correct check digit. The API renders the supplied identifier. Code 128 supports up to 80 printable ASCII characters. QR input supports up to 500 characters. One image uses one generation unit.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Paid ZIP batch generation</h2><p><code>POST /v1/barcodes/batch-render</code> accepts an <code>items</code> array of single-image request objects and returns a ZIP archive. Starter supports up to 25 images per request and 2,000 generated images per month. Growth supports up to 100 per request and 10,000 per month. Each image consumes one generation unit. Single and batch generation share the account's generation balance. Free and one-time lookup-pack accounts support single-image generation.</p><p>The API checks all items before reserving generation units. An invalid item fails the entire batch. Filenames are generated as barcode-001.svg or barcode-001.png and continue in input order. The <code>batch_generation_max</code> field in the usage response reports your plan's per-request maximum.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Create printable labels</h2><p>Send this JSON to <code>POST /v1/labels/render</code>. The response is an <code>application/pdf</code> document. Choose <code>a4</code> or <code>letter</code> paper. Each sheet has two columns and five rows. The document accepts up to 100 labels including copies. Each copy uses one label unit.</p><CodeBlock label="PDF label request body" language="json" code={labels} /><p>For CSV input, send a <code>csv_text</code> body to <code>POST /v1/labels/from-csv</code>. Required column is <code>barcode</code>. Optional columns are <code>symbology</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>detail</code> and <code>copies</code>. CSV labels use A4. Product metadata can be supplied in the title and detail fields. These text fields support printable Latin characters, including common accented letters and currency symbols. Long text is shortened with an ellipsis. Very long Code 128 values may exceed the printable width of this template.</p><p>Print at actual size and test alignment on plain paper before using label stock. The <a href="/barcode-labels/">label printing tool</a> provides the same CSV workflow in your browser.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Preview and enrich a barcode CSV</h2><p>Send the following body to <code>POST /v1/products/enrichment-preview</code> to count rows, invalid identifiers and matches in the current local catalog. Preview is rate limited and consumes no enrichment units. It reports the enrichment balance and the units needed to process the file.</p><CodeBlock label="CSV request body" language="json" code={csv} /><p>Send the same body to <code>POST /v1/products/enrich-csv</code> to download an enriched CSV. Processing can use configured fallback sources in addition to local data. Each input row uses one enrichment unit, including duplicate, unmatched and invalid rows. Each request accepts up to 100 rows, 50 columns and a 500,000-character CSV body. The browser tool also limits file size to 500 KB.</p><p>The input requires a <code>barcode</code> column. Output adds lookup_status, lookup_name, lookup_brand, lookup_quantity and lookup_image_url. Preserve leading zeros as text. Output cells that could execute as spreadsheet formulas are prefixed with an apostrophe. Optional product fields may be blank.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Track separate service allowances</h2><p><code>GET /v1/services/usage</code> returns generation, labels and enrichment balances for the API key's account. Keys share their account's balances. These monthly tool counters reset at 00:00 UTC on the first day of each calendar month. Existing product lookup allowances follow their own plan rules.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Monthly units</th><th>Free / One-time</th><th>Starter</th><th>Growth</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Generated images</td><td>100</td><td>2,000</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Images per ZIP request</td><td>Single images</td><td>25</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Printed labels</td><td>25</td><td>500</td><td>2,500</td></tr><tr><td>Enrichment rows</td><td>250</td><td>2,000</td><td>5,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Successful processing responses include <code>X-Service-Category</code>, <code>X-Service-Quota-Limit</code>, <code>X-Service-Quota-Remaining</code> and <code>X-Service-Quota-Period</code>. The usage endpoint reports the configured values for your account. Limits can be customized by the service operator.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Handle errors and retries</h2><p>Invalid payloads return 422 before units are reserved. Missing or invalid keys return 401. An exhausted service allowance returns 429 with the error code <code>service_quota_exceeded</code> and the category. Request-rate limits are tracked independently for lookup, generation, labels and enrichment.</p><p>Image and label output is rendered before units are charged. CSV enrichment reserves its row allowance before product resolution. An interrupted processing request may already have consumed units. These POST endpoints create a new operation on every call. Inspect usage before resubmitting, and avoid automatic retries on an uncertain response.</p></section>
<section><h2>Signed-in website access</h2><p>All interactive tools require an account. The generator uses the account session on <code>/v1/account/barcodes/render</code> and <code>/v1/account/barcodes/batch-render</code>. It shares the same balances as API-key requests. The account needs an active API key for attribution, which registration creates. The website displays the remaining balance from <code>/v1/account/services/usage</code>. Cookie requests must originate from a configured website origin.</p></section>  <section><h2>Try the tools</h2><p><a href="/barcode-generator/">Create an account to generate barcodes</a>, <a href="/barcode-labels/">print CSV labels</a>, or <a href="/csv-product-enrichment/">preview a product spreadsheet</a>. For programmatic access, <a href="/register/">create an account</a> and generate an API key.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
